<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.themostafaosamadev.Riwaq-Reader</id>
  <name>Riwaq</name>
  <summary>A calm, offline-first e-book reader</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.themostafaosamadev">
    <name>Mostafa Osama</name>
  </developer>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.themostafaosamadev.Riwaq-Reader.desktop</launchable>
  <description>
    <p>
      Riwaq is an e-book reader for EPUB, PDF and DOCX, built for long reading
      sessions and for Arabic as a first-class script rather than an
      afterthought. It keeps your library on your own machine: no account, no
      sync, no analytics.
    </p>
    <p>Reading:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>EPUB, PDF and DOCX, with a reflowable reader and a fixed-page reader</li>
      <li>Sixteen bundled font families across Naskh, modern sans, Kufi and display faces</li>
      <li>Full typographic control: size, line height, letter and paragraph spacing, width, alignment, hyphenation</li>
      <li>Highlights and notes, a contents panel, and a progress scrubber</li>
      <li>Focus mode for reading without chrome</li>
      <li>Right-to-left throughout, with an Arabic interface</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The bundled fonts are licensed separately under the SIL Open Font
      License 1.1.
    </p>
  </description>
